  "appliesTo": "Term dates for community and voluntary controlled schools are set by the local authority in consultation with neighbouring authorities and groups representing school staff.",
  "academyNote": "In foundation, voluntary aided, academies, and residential special schools, it is the governing body that decides the beginning and the end of school terms and holidays.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "Wiltshire has a longer October break: term 1 ends on a Wednesday (21 October 2026, 20 October 2027) and term 2 starts on the Monday a week and a half later.",
      "source": "https://www.wiltshire.gov.uk/article/1684/School-term-dates-and-holidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Schools in the Mere and Tisbury area may choose between Wiltshire and Dorset dates.",
      "source": "https://www.wiltshire.gov.uk/article/1684/School-term-dates-and-holidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "All five staff development days (or the equivalent of 30 hours) are set at each school's discretion and are taken within the 195 published term days.",
      "source": "https://www.wiltshire.gov.uk/article/1684/School-term-dates-and-holidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council publishes six terms with a day count for each: 37, 35, 30, 24, 34 and 35 days in 2026-27, a total of 195.",
      "source": "https://www.wiltshire.gov.uk/article/1684/School-term-dates-and-holidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Dates are set in consultation with neighbouring authorities and groups representing school staff.",
      "source": "https://www.wiltshire.gov.uk/article/1684/School-term-dates-and-holidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2026-27 year starts on Tuesday 1 September 2026, and the 2027-28 summer term runs to Tuesday 25 July 2028.",
      "source": "https://www.wiltshire.gov.uk/article/1684/School-term-dates-and-holidays"
    }
  ],
